    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "E. BROWN Jr. DEL\nLENGTH OF YEET\nLENGTH ON DEeY\nLENGTH OVERALL (FROM NIGHT HEADS TO TAFFRAIL) 235 FEET\nEncored aciding to at of Congres in the your 1852 6y ATin in the Clad Offer of the Sumed Come of Nam Yad\nTa Mess Grinnell. Minturn g Co This Print of their Splendid\nCLIPPER SHIP \"FLYING CLOUD.\nis Rospoctfully dodicated by the Publisher.\nNEW YORK, PUBLISHED BY N. CURRIER. 152 NASSAU STREET\nLITH RY N. CURRIED\nPEE\n21½ FEET\nTONNAGE PER REGISTER\nBUILT BI DONALD MeKAY AT EAST BOSTON. MASS 1AS",
      "CLIPPER\nSHIP \"FLYING CLOUD\"\nThe front cover of this menu is a reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives clipper ship print.\nCurrier \u0026 Ives, known as the \"Printmakers of America\", graphically preserved the glorious clipper\nship era in a magnificent series of clipper ship prints. This print, one of a series, is being reproduced\nthrough the courtesy of The Museum of the City of New York.\nLaunched in 1851, the \"Flying Cloud\" was the largest merchant ship afloat. In her brief career\nthe \"Flying Cloud\" was perhaps the greatest and the tallest of the China clippers. She set a half-\ndozen of the world's permanent sailing records, and reaped huge profits, once making nearly $200,000\non a single voyage. On her maiden run to California, the \"Flying Cloud\" sped to the Golden Gate\nin 89 days. Thereafter eighty-nine was the magic number for every other clipper captain.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers* of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the lanes of com-\nmerce to all the far places of the world... to Japan... to Australia... and, in the days of the great\ngold rush, from America's east coast, around Cape Horn, South America, to California. Our current\nequipment... the Clipper fleet of the Twentieth Century\n.. consists of the finest commercial\naircraft ever developed—aircraft that have helped us establish an unparalleled record for safety,\nspeed and service.\n\"CLIPPER TRADE MARK-REG U.S. PAT OFFICE - COPYRIGHT 1966 PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS INC\nLITHO IN USA -8739-0393\n2000.058.0581"
